---
/*
 * A real page built with the layout, outside the Starlight content collection:
 * the layout renders its own document, so it cannot be embedded in a docs page.
 */
import BlogArticle from "astro-nosferatu/layouts/BlogArticle.astro";
---

<BlogArticle
	title="Nosferatu, a sympathy for the night"
	description="A worked example of the BlogArticle layout, rendered as its own document."
	lang="en"
	imageSocialMedia="/og/blog-article.png"
>
	<p>
		This page is the whole document the layout produced. Everything above — the
		heading and the paragraph under it — comes from the layout's
		<code>title</code> and <code>description</code> props; everything from here
		down is the default slot.
	</p>
	<p>
		View the source of this page: its head is <code>BaseHead</code>, so it
		carries the canonical URL, the favicon link and the Open Graph and Twitter
		tags — including the image passed as
		<code>imageSocialMedia</code>. Target
		<code>.nf-layout-blog-article</code> from your own stylesheet to style the
		body.
	</p>
	<h2>Slot content is ordinary markup</h2>
	<p>
		Headings, lists and components all render inside the <code>article</code>,
		after the description paragraph, in the order they were written.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			The document title is the <code>title</code> prop.
		</li>
		<li>
			The page description metadata is the <code>description</code> prop.
		</li>
		<li>Nothing else is added around them.</li>
	</ul>
	<h2>Three fonts, three jobs</h2>
	<p>
		This paragraph is set in Plus Jakarta Sans at weight 400, and so is
		<strong>this emphasis</strong>, which stays bolder than the text around it,
		and <a href="/styles/">this link</a>. The heading above it is in Outfit, the
		page's general font, because headings inherit from
		<code>body</code> instead of taking the article font.
	</p>
	<pre><code>const font = 'Geist Mono'; // a code block renders in it too</code></pre>
	<p>
		None of this is loaded by the library: the docs site installs the three
		Fontsource packages itself. Without them every stack falls back to a system
		font.
	</p>
</BlogArticle>
